
# Minecraft Skin Extractor

View and extract the skin caches downloaded from the Minecraft servers you join.

## Screenshots 

![Screenshot](screenshots/main-window.png)

## Getting Started
### Requirements
- Python 3.10+ (tested on 3.10)

> **Note:** If you're not using Windows, you'll need to install the dependencies manually and run the application using Python.

### Installation
**Option 1: Download ZIP**

1. Go to the [latest release](https://github.com/Kuppiarda/minecraft-skin-extractor/releases).
2. Download and extract the ZIP file.
3. Open the extracted project folder.
4. Run `setup.bat` or manually install the dependencies using `pip install -r requirements.txt`

**Option 2: Clone with Git**
```
git clone https://github.com/Kuppiarda/minecraft-skin-extractor.git
cd minecraft-skin-extractor
setup.bat
```

## Running
1. Run `run_ui.bat` or activate the virtual environment and execute `python main.py`.

